WHAT THIS LICENSE COVERS, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT

This license applies to the *derived layer* authored here: the summaries,
cross-talk syntheses, concept definitions, maturity labels, speaker pages,
corpus structure, and the selection and arrangement of the material.

It does NOT apply to the underlying talks. This wiki quotes AI Engineer World's
Fair 2026 speakers in excerpt, with attribution and a deep link to the source
video at the exact timestamp on the conference's own YouTube channel. Copyright
in those talks — and in the quoted words themselves — belongs to the speakers
and to the AI Engineer World's Fair. Nothing here grants you rights to that
material, and the CC BY grant above cannot and does not extend to it.

This repository deliberately ships no full transcripts. Excerpts plus deep links
are intended to send readers to the original talks rather than substitute for
them.

If you are a speaker or a conference organizer and want a quote, a page, or an
attribution corrected or removed, please open an issue on the repository.

Code in this repository is licensed separately under the MIT License — see the
`LICENSE` file at the repository root.
